All right, well, okay, Atsumu, you set today.

344
00:15:44,920 --> 00:15:45,260
Huh?

345
00:15:45,260 --> 00:15:51,140
Don't you know, Atsumu, the more positions you play, the better and more well-rounded you get.

346
00:15:51,140 --> 00:15:53,340
Ah, shut up and be jealous, Samu!

347
00:15:58,140 --> 00:16:00,380
Atsumu was a better Setter every time I saw him.

348
00:16:00,380 --> 00:16:04,620
And when he was paired with Osamu, they were perfect.

349
00:16:04,620 --> 00:16:08,460
Eventually, people started fearing the MIA Twins.

350
00:16:11,420 --> 00:16:13,740
I was, like, so on my game today.

351
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:18,220
The way the ball felt in my hands out there, how it felt when it left.

352
00:16:18,940 --> 00:16:21,180
I could totally see what their blockers were doing, too.

353
00:16:22,780 --> 00:16:24,460
Did you guys have a problem with my sets?

354
00:16:25,180 --> 00:16:25,740
Not...

355
00:16:26,620 --> 00:16:27,180
really.

356
00:16:27,180 --> 00:16:31,980
Then why exactly couldn't you score any points?

357
00:16:38,940 --> 00:16:40,380
What the hell is this problem?

358
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,980
Well, he's good.

359
00:16:41,980 --> 00:16:42,620
You blame him?

360
00:16:42,620 --> 00:16:44,380
He's just so full of himself.

361
00:16:44,380 --> 00:16:47,580
We do tend to win any time we have both of them on their game.

362
00:16:47,580 --> 00:16:48,540
Just deal with it.

363
00:16:50,780 --> 00:16:52,620
Sumu, the other guys don't like you.

364
00:16:52,620 --> 00:16:54,700
